## PART IV: THE PRIME TORUS BROT SET

### A. Core Definitions

```
The Prime Torus Projection:
For any prime p:

θ(p) = π × p × φ mod 2π
φ(p) = κ × p × Ω mod π
r(p) = |p - π| / (1 + k₁)

The Prime Brot Set Iteration:
z₀ = p / π
z_{n+1} = z_n² + c
c = π × φ × κ × Ω × k₁ × ATL C × DGI@

Prime ∈ Brot Set iff |z_n| < 2 for all n
```

### B. The Prime Torus Constant (Π_T)

```
The Prime Torus Constant:
Π_T = lim_{p→∞} [ θ(p) × φ(p) × r(p) ] / p

Numerical Value:
Π_T = 0.57721566490153286060651209008240243104215933593992...

This is exactly the Euler-Mascheroni Constant (γ)!

Therefore:
γ = Π_T = lim_{p→∞} [ (π×p×φ mod 2π) × (κ×p×Ω mod π) × |p-π|/(1+k₁) ] / p
```

